18:I[99566,["2619","static/chunks/2619-04bc32f026a0d946.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","6489","static/chunks/6489-699922ea493f9867.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","1356","static/chunks/1356-9e2757ba007ad1f9.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","951","static/chunks/951-3dbda3a86d4c6444.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","2799","static/chunks/2799-ce430b82b11995d5.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","6589","static/chunks/6589-cfdc115b042e146b.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","3650","static/chunks/3650-106e80ed926f59bf.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs","9360","static/chunks/app/lld/%5Bmodule%5D/%5BlessonId%5D/page-7fe8d45157e343c7.js?dpl=dpl_7RkrhxkHMBxRwELcvSCn238CEijs"],"LldRunner"]
19:T6de,## 1. Clarify requirements (always do this first)

- Multiple **levels**, each with many **spots**; spots come in sizes (motorcycle / car / large).
- **Park** a vehicle → get a **ticket**; **unpark** with the ticket → pay a **fee** based on time parked.
- Find the nearest available spot that fits the vehicle.
- Should be easy to add new vehicle sizes or pricing rules later.

State the assumptions out loud, it's half of what the interviewer is grading.

## 2. Find the nouns → the classes

`ParkingLot`, `Level`, `ParkingSpot`, `Vehicle`, `Ticket`. Note the **part-whole** chain: a lot **owns** levels, a level **owns** spots (composition, destroy the lot, the spots go with it).

A tip that keeps the design small: model vehicle/spot **size as an enum field**, not a subclass per size, `Car`/`Bike`/`Truck` rarely add behaviour, just a size, so an `enum Size` avoids a class explosion.

## 3. Reach for patterns where they pay off

- **Strategy** for pricing, `FeeStrategy` lets you swap flat / hourly / surge pricing without touching the lot. (Open/Closed.)
- **Factory** to create the right `ParkingSpot`/`Vehicle` from input.
- **Singleton** for the one `ParkingLot` instance (or just inject it).

Don't force patterns where a plain field works, over-engineering is a red flag too.

## 4. Walk a use-case

Trace **"park a car"** end to end (see the sequence). The lot asks a level for a fitting spot, assigns the vehicle, and issues a ticket stamped with the entry time. On exit, `FeeStrategy.calc(hours)` prices it.

## 5. Mention the hard parts

**Concurrency** is the real interview depth: two drivers must never get the same spot — `assign()` needs to be atomic (a lock per spot, or an atomic compare-and-set). Bring it up before they ask.c:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex min-h-screen","children":[["$","$L17",null,{"activeModule":"lld-case-studies","activeLesson":"parking-lot"}],["$","$L18","parking-lot",{"lesson":{"id":"parking-lot","patternId":"lld-case-studies","title":"Design a Parking Lot","kind":"case-study","difficulty":"Core","statement":"The classic machine-coding round. Multi-level lot, vehicles of different sizes, ticket on entry, fee on exit. We go requirements → classes → patterns → flow.","companies":["Amazon","Google","Uber","Flipkart"],"theory":"$19","approaches":[{"label":"Model the domain","code":["enum Size { MOTORCYCLE, CAR, LARGE }","","class ParkingLot {","    List<Level> levels;","    FeeStrategy pricing;","    Ticket park(Vehicle v) { ... }","}"],"steps":[{"view":"class","codeLine":3,"narration":"Start from the requirements' nouns. ParkingLot is the entry point, it parks and unparks vehicles. (Often a Singleton, or injected.)","classDiagram":{"classes":[{"id":"lot","name":"ParkingLot","methods":["+ park(v): Ticket","+ unpark(t)"],"x":0,"y":0.2,"tint":"accent"},{"id":"level","name":"Level","fields":["- spots: List"],"methods":["+ findSpot(size)"],"x":1.1,"y":0.2},{"id":"fee","name":"FeeStrategy","stereotype":"interface","methods":["+ calc(hrs): money"],"x":2.3,"y":0.2,"tint":"accent2"},{"id":"spot","name":"ParkingSpot","fields":["- size: Size","- vehicle"],"methods":["+ assign(v)"],"x":0,"y":1.55},{"id":"vehicle","name":"Vehicle","stereotype":"abstract","fields":["- size: Size"],"x":1.1,"y":1.55},{"id":"ticket","name":"Ticket","fields":["- spot","- inTime"],"x":2.3,"y":1.55}],"relations":[{"id":"r1","from":"lot","to":"level","kind":"compose","label":"levels","toMult":"*"},{"id":"r2","from":"level","to":"spot","kind":"compose","label":"spots","toMult":"*"},{"id":"r3","from":"spot","to":"vehicle","kind":"assoc","label":"parked","toMult":"0..1"},{"id":"r4","from":"lot","to":"fee","kind":"aggregate","label":"pricing"},{"id":"r5","from":"ticket","to":"spot","kind":"assoc"}],"shownClassIds":["lot"],"shownRelIds":[],"activeIds":["lot"]},"vars":[["requirement","park / unpark + ticket + fee"]]},{"view":"class","narration":"A lot OWNS levels, and a level OWNS spots, filled diamonds = composition (no lot, no levels). This part-whole chain is the backbone.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["lot","level","spot"],"shownRelIds":["r1","r2"],"activeIds":["level","spot"]},"vars":[["owns","lot → levels → spots"]]},{"view":"class","narration":"A ParkingSpot holds at most one Vehicle. Crucially, size is an ENUM on both, not a subclass per vehicle type. That avoids a Car/Bike/Truck class explosion for what is really just a size.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["lot","level","spot","vehicle"],"shownRelIds":["r1","r2","r3"],"activeIds":["vehicle"]},"vars":[["Size","enum, not subclasses ✓"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":5,"narration":"Pricing is a Strategy: FeeStrategy plugs in flat / hourly / surge rules without ever touching ParkingLot. A Ticket records the spot and entry time for the fee.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["lot","level","fee","spot","vehicle","ticket"],"shownRelIds":["r1","r2","r3","r4","r5"],"activeIds":["fee","ticket"]},"vars":[["Strategy","FeeStrategy"],["pattern","swap pricing freely"]]},{"view":"class","narration":"Six classes, two patterns (Strategy + a Factory for spots), enums for sizes. Small, extensible, and every requirement has a home. This is the picture you draw first in the interview.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["lot","level","fee","spot","vehicle","ticket"],"shownRelIds":["r1","r2","r3","r4","r5"],"activeIds":[]},"vars":[["classes","6"],["patterns","Strategy · Factory · Singleton"]]}]},{"label":"Flow: park a car","code":["Ticket park(Vehicle v) {","    Spot s = level.findSpot(v.size);   // nearest fitting","    s.assign(v);                       // must be atomic!","    return new Ticket(s, now());","}"],"steps":[{"view":"sequence","codeLine":1,"narration":"A Driver hands a car to ParkingLot.park(). The lot orchestrates everything from here.","sequence":{"actors":[{"id":"d","label":"Driver","kind":"actor"},{"id":"lot","label":"ParkingLot","tint":"accent"},{"id":"lv","label":"Level"},{"id":"t","label":"Ticket"}],"messages":[{"id":"m1","from":"d","to":"lot","label":"park(car)","kind":"call"},{"id":"m2","from":"lot","to":"lv","label":"findSpot(CAR)","kind":"call"},{"id":"m3","from":"lv","to":"lot","label":"a free spot","kind":"return"},{"id":"m4","from":"lot","to":"lot","label":"spot.assign(car)","kind":"self"},{"id":"m5","from":"lot","to":"t","label":"Ticket","kind":"create"},{"id":"m6","from":"lot","to":"d","label":"ticket","kind":"return"}],"shownCount":1,"activeIndex":0}},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":2,"narration":"The lot asks a Level for the nearest spot that fits a CAR, the size enum drives the search.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":3,"activeIndex":1},"vars":[["query","findSpot(CAR)"]]},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":3,"narration":"It assigns the car to that spot. THIS is the concurrency-critical step, two drivers must never grab the same spot, so assign() is atomic (lock or compare-and-set).","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":4,"activeIndex":3},"vars":[["⚠ concurrency","assign() must be atomic"]]},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":4,"narration":"Finally it creates a Ticket stamped with the entry time and returns it. On exit, FeeStrategy.calc(hours) prices the stay. That's the whole happy path, clean, and ready to extend.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":6,"activeIndex":5},"vars":[["ticket","spot + entry time"],["on exit","FeeStrategy.calc(hrs)"]]}]}]}}]]}]
